{"type":"text","timestamp":1794318904227,"sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6b3effetosjIkRTOmK673","part":{"id":"prt_1c5bdab830010AibwIjhLuwJ95","messageID":"msg_1c5bd9192001j6NYqeqXip3iCA","sessionID":"ses_e3a4b6b3effetosjIkRTOmK673","type":"text","text":"Done. The todo app is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask with SQLite under `./data`, token-based auth (Bearer tokens stored per-user), and the full `/api/auth/*` + `/api/todos` CRUD. Todos are scoped to the owner (`user_id`), `completed_at` is set/cleared on toggle, listing orders open-first → due date → newest, with `completed`/`priority`/`page`/`page_size` filters and the `{items, total, page, page_size, remaining}` envelope.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 (via `@tailwindcss/vite`), with register/sign-in forms, sign-out, the todo list with priority badges, overdue highlighting, immediate-save checkboxes, open counter, tabs, priority filter, load-more, add form, inline editing, and delete confirmation.\n\nVerification:\n- All API behaviors tested via Flask test client (auth, validation errors, isolation between users, paging/filters, `completed_at` lifecycle).\n- Gunicorn booted, served `GET /api/health`, register, and the built frontend correctly.\n- `npm run build` produces `frontend/dist`.\n\nOne note: the sandbox's pip 25.1.1 fails on `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` (a constraints+hashes bug), so I verified the backend by installing the pinned packages directly. The repo's `requirements.lock` is unchanged and your code adds no new backend dependencies, so the `Dockerfile` build path is unaffected.","time":{"start":1794318904195,"end":1794318904199}}}
